# American English spelling

## Rule

Prose, JSDoc, and our own identifiers use American English, never British spellings:

| American (use this)                                                                                                                                                                                                       | Never the British equivalent |
| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- |
| `color`                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | ✓                            |
| `optimization`, `optimize`                                                                                                                                                                                                | ✓                            |
| `canceled`, `canceling`                                                                                                                                                                                                   | ✓                            |
| `center`, `centered`                                                                                                                                                                                                      | ✓                            |
| `behavior`                                                                                                                                                                                                                | ✓                            |
| `traveling`                                                                                                                                                                                                               | ✓                            |
| `normalize`, `initialize`, `serialize`, `recognize`, `organize`, `customize`, `analyze`, `finalize`, `minimize`, `maximize`, `prioritize`, `categorize`, `synchronize`, `standardize`, `specialize`, `utilize`, `realize` | ✓                            |

## Exemptions – do not "fix" these

Literal third-party or spec-mandated identifiers that are correctly spelled with a British `s` or `c` in their own spec
must be left exactly as the spec defines them:

- Web Audio API: `AnalyserNode`, `createAnalyser()`
- This repo's own `gray`/`grey` named-color alias in `src/utils/Color32.ts` (`alias('grey', 'gray')`), which
  deliberately mirrors the CSS Color Module's own dual spelling (`gray`/`grey`, `darkgray`/`darkgrey`, ...)

Full policy: `CLAUDE.md` (American English spelling). Applies to doc prose too — see `.cursor/rules/docs-authoring.mdc`
(Documentation authoring style).
